WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.960
Many of you have requested us to make a video
about France: on of the wealthiest countries

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.630
and, yet, one with the hardest economic problems
in the entire World. Today, France is the

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:23.990
second economic power in the European Union.
But that might last less that we might think.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.331
Their young unemployment rate is over a 23%
and their public debt is twice as big as their

00:00:28.331 --> 00:00:37.809
entire GDP. Just 15 years ago, the whole world
was buying Renault cars or Alcatel mobile

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:44.260
phones. Today, French exports have fallen
to half of what they used to be. Their companies

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:49.250
can´t face the competition of their rivals
in China, South Korea or even United States

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:58.250
and Germany.
And as you can imagine, this economic crisis

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.440
has a reflexion on society. If you don´t
believe me, just look at their presidential

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:09.710
elections of this 2017. None of the candidates
from the traditional parties has made it to

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:14.229
the second round. Most of the French voters
are fed up with their political stablishment

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:18.780
and this is why they´ve chosen a politician
who wants to make a 180º shift in the French

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.329
system.
So now you might wonder: What are the reasons

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:29.729
behind this French crisis? And most importantly
What does Macron propose to solve it? Today

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:38.479
we are gonna answer to this question. But
before, let´s take a look at history.

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:40.299
FRANCE IS TO THE FRENCH PEOPLE

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:43.889
Right after the Wold War II, all the European
countries were on bankrupcy. France was one

00:01:43.889 --> 00:01:50.560
of them. Half of the country was destroyed
by the bombs and this included houses aswell

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.119
as factories and growths. Luckily enough,
Uncle Sam was ready to help. At the end of

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:03.990
the day, United States was interested to have
a strong Europe to buy all their goods. This

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:11.930
is why the so called MARSHALL PLAN was a big
injection of billions of dollars for all the

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:15.590
European nations to be reconstructed.
But hold on a minute! Because each of this

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:19.980
countries used this finance in different ways.
For instance, German Government created their

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.600
own political theory: the ORDO LIBERALISM,
AKA, social liberalism. This was a combination

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.110
of social programs and free enterprise. In
other words, the Government would provide

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:35.160
a safety net for their citizens and subsidize
the companies. But, on the other hand, those

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:41.860
companies where private and they could compete
to each other.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.730
France was the opposite case. The president
back then, General Charles de Gaulle, was

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.980
no friend of free enterprise. So his political
theory, the DIRIGISME, was pretty different

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.070
from that of the Germans.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.040
“This cabinet is not for giving proposals
but to give orders”

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.040
–Charles de Gaulle

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.790
So de Gaulle used all this Money from US to
nationalize almost all the big corporations.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.720
Steel factories, electrical companies, phone
companies… even those car-maker behemoths

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.010
as RENAULT, PEAUGEOT or CITROEN had the Government
as the biggest shareholder.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.560
But not only that! They also created a DIRIGISTE
system on society, where The State would play

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.250
a major role in all the areas, including the
conditions to hire workers or the minimal

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.750
wage. This is very important for you to understand.
Because not all the welfare states are created

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.920
the same. In Germany, for instance, there
is no minimal wage and there is a bigger space

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:35.760
for trade unions and companies to negociate
contract conditions. Healthcare is provided

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.810
by private insurance. And the regional governments
have a lot to say when it comes to laws and

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:44.490
regulations. Nevertheless, in France, ALL
of the social politics come from the Central

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.490
Authority.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:54.210
In other words, De Gaulle represents the opposite
to what we like here at VisualPolitik.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:58.010
But despite all of that, during this first
years after the World War II, France entered

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:03.400
the so called “Glory thirties”. In this
3 decades, the average wage tripled and those

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:14.069
companies, sponsored by the Government, became
global leaders. Just for your understanding,

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:18.130
way before American companies started moving
their factories to China, Renault and Michelin

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.530
where opening facilities in Spain, where salaries
where much lower.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.470
But let´s be honest, during that time, every
European country was growing at the same rhythm.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:30.770
Just think about it. We are talking about
the 60s. Asia was not the economic powerhouse

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:37.620
it is today. Latino America was full of dictatorships
of all kinds. And the Soviet Union could not

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.580
produce quality goods to sell in the international
market. Nonetheless, France had an important

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:48.530
industrial tradition, a well educated society
and, over all, rule of law and a stable political

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:54.779
system for companies.

00:04:54.779 --> 00:05:00.490
Not only that! In 1958, those countries, already
rebuilt by the Plan Marshall decided to create

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:05.409
a Free Trade Union, which would become the
European Union. In this moment, France had

00:05:05.409 --> 00:05:11.620
the biggest population. Don´t forget that,
back in the time, Germany was divided in two

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:17.020
halfs. This means they were in the strongest
position to negotiate their entering conditions.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.639
And as I said, Charles de Gaulle was no good
friend of free trade. So he used his power

00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:25.150
to make France the dominating country in certain
industries like agriculture.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.839
Bien entendu, on peut sauter sur sa chaise
comme un cabri en disant l’Europe ! l’Europe

00:05:26.839 --> 00:05:28.090
! l’Europe ! mais cela n’aboutit à rien
et cela ne signifie rien.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:33.080
“One can shout Europe!, Europe!, Europe!,
but it doesn´t help to anything, nor means

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.080
anything”–Charles de Gaulle

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.789
If you are watching this video from anywhere
in Europe, you might have heard about Common

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:43.139
Agricultural Policy. This is a policy created
to keep European consumers to buy agricultural

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:48.509
goods to the third World. But not only that!
It also imposes production quotas INSIDE of

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:53.440
the European area. This means Polish or a
Spanish farmers cannot produce or sell all

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:59.409
the milk they want. They must meet some maximum
quotas imposed by Brussels. So guess what,

00:05:59.409 --> 00:06:03.580
this is a French invention. And this explains
things like this one.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:10.789
“With a base price value of €70.4 billion
in 2011, French agricultural production is

00:06:10.789 --> 00:06:14.430
the leader in Europe.”

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:19.169
De Gaulle held power during decades. But the
rest of the French presidents have kept this

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:24.460
DIRIGISTE model. At the end of the day, during
the 60s and the 70s, France was on fire. So

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:32.249
if something works… Why should you fix it?
Mmmm Now we are gonna tell you why.

00:06:32.249 --> 00:06:34.279
SAME SOLUTIONS TO A DIFFERENT PROBLEM

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:38.740
The problem starts when the rest of the world
runs faster than you. We are talking about

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:43.180
the 80s and the 90s. The Berlin Wall fell
down, China started opening their economy

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:48.520
and lots of new countries, like Spain or Greece,
became members of the European Union. And

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:54.289
of course, they also wanted to sell their
products. In other words, out of a sudden,

00:06:54.289 --> 00:07:13.580
France had rivals. And this is what explains
why this kind of news are so common.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:20.150
The same happens with other industries. Take
a look at this chart that represents the trade

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:28.840
balance in France. If you pay attention, you
can see how, after the 90s, the exports are

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:33.509
dropping slowly. This trend is specially strong
after the finantial crisis.

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:41.949
Do you remember ALCATEL phones? When the mobile
phones started becoming a thing, Alcatel was

00:07:41.949 --> 00:07:50.999
a juggernaut in this industry. Now, they have
just disappeared in a market dominated by

00:07:50.999 --> 00:07:55.580
American, Chinese and South Korean companies.
And this is just one example of how France

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.370
is losing their innovation track.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.139
And now you might wonder… what has been
the answer of all the different French governments

00:08:03.139 --> 00:08:08.229
to all of this? Well, they just kept protecting
their companies from the rest of the world.

00:08:08.229 --> 00:08:11.220
For instance, other countries like Sweden
had big like VOLVO CARS. Nonetheless, when

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.860
a Chinese Fund wanted to buy part of this
firm, Government didn´t intervene at all.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:22.710
They had it clear the separation between business
and State. We cannot say the same in France.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:27.220
Just look at what happened when PEPSI wanted
to buy DANONE in 2005.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:33.979
“Jean-Louis Borloo, the labour minister,
said the government will do "all we can" to

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:39.000
oppose a bid, and Thierry Breton, the finance
minister, pledged to protect Danone.”

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.160
But this is not the only thing that doesn´t
change in France. Their social spending is

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:48.100
still the highest in all across European Union.
Even bigger than that of the Nordic countries.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:53.790
And the French Administration employs more
civil servants than any other European Country.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.080
And their salaries are pretty generous.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.850
In other words: France has a lower income
but keeps spending the same as they did during

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.470
the Glory days. This explains why their public
debt is growing as much as it does.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:12.900
But hold on a second! Because now it seems
things are starting to change!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.900
MACRON´S QUIET REVOLUTION?

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.860
Yes, we know it. One thing is what a politician
promises during the elections and another

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:22.580
one is what he or she actually does. But there
is something we have to admit in the case

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:27.970
of Macron: his program is a complete breakup
with French Dirigisme. All the political analyst

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:33.440
have labelled this man as a moderate politicians
who wants to continue the work of his predecessors.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.280
But… is that really true?
The truth is some of his proposals are absolutely

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:55.620
have never been heard by other French president,
nor a right winger, nor a left winger.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.650
For a better understanding, in a electoral
campaign that became famous by the populist

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:06.040
tone of Mrs. Le Pen, Mr. Macron is proposing
to retire over 120.000 civil servants. Yes,

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:11.550
many of you might thing this is horrible.
But there is something we must admit: he is

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:18.240
being honest. There is no other politician
who would suggest such an impopular thing

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:23.260
during the elections. Nonetheless, Macron
has won this election by suggesting the opposite

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:28.440
of what a candidate should do. On his manifesto
he also promises he will never reduce the

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:34.050
retirement age. In other words, he is really
commited to reduce French public spending.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:41.360
On the other hand, Macron combines all this
Budget cuts with lowering taxes and helping

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:45.680
small companies. On his own words, Macron
wants to substitute the French dirigisme by

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:50.700
a model closer to that one of Germany or Sweden,
where welfare states coexists with free market

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:51.700
economy.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:55.160
And now you might wonder… even after winning
the elections… Does he have actual power

00:10:55.160 --> 00:11:00.730
to make this happen? In France, the President
has not so much power as in America. And every

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:06.350
law he wants to pass should go through the
parliament. And… Who is the biggest political

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.350
force on this parliament?

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:12.180
Well… the truth is we will not know it until
this summer. This June of 2017, French people

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:16.730
will go back to the voting stations. This
time they will hold legislative elections.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:23.080
And here, the party of Marine Le Pen, the
NATIONAL FRONT, has bigger changes to become

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:30.460
the main force. But… what does the French
far right wing want? Well… if you wanna

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:37.500
know it, you should click on this video.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.870
And now the question is Do you really believe
this quiet revolution of Emmanuel Macron can

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:47.360
put France out of the hole? Do you think French
stagnation has a solution? You can leave your

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:50.220
answer in the comments below.

